      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for tracing this. The millivolt is lost in the device, not in the daemon. The daemon resends what was last requested rather than what the device reports, so repeated writes do not keep lowering the other two, but it does not add the millivolt back, since that would be wrong on a device that holds what it is written. Before anything has been requested, the first write after a restart can still move them by a millivolt.",
